{"results":[{"url":"https://www.jsonline.com/story/news/politics/2020/01/14/appeals-court-blocks-purge-wisconsin-voter-rolls-time-being/4465158002/","final_url":"https://www.jsonline.com/story/news/politics/2020/01/14/appeals-court-blocks-purge-wisconsin-voter-rolls-time-being/4465158002/?gnt-cfr=1&gca-cat=p&gca-uir=false&gca-epti=z1192xxu002771e1192xxv002471&gca-ft=22&gca-ds=sophi&gnt-djm=1","title":"Appeals court blocks purge of Wisconsin voter rolls for the time being","description":"An appeals court ordered the state to keep more than 200,000 people on its voter rolls Tuesday.","language":"en","text":"POLITICS\n\n# Appeals court blocks purge of Wisconsin voter rolls for the time being\n\nPatrick Marley\n\nMilwaukee Journal Sentinel\n\nUpdated Jan. 14, 2020, 9:24 p.m. CT\n\nMADISON - An appeals court ordered the state to keep more than 200,000 people on its voter rolls Tuesday, a day after an Ozaukee County judge found election officials in contempt of court for not following his December decision to suspend voter registrations.","author":"Patrick Marley","published_date":"2020-01-14T17:08:31Z","latency_ms":970.2086709985451,"format":"markdown"}],"errors":[]}